WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.567
Make the QuickBooks export file.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:11.000
QuickBooks export. Until QuickBooks is connected directly, the office sends it files. Open the export panel.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:19.400
Where it goes. In QuickBooks Online: Settings, then Import data. This line also says when you last exported.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:27.267
Customers first. Export customers before invoices, so every invoice finds its customer in QuickBooks.

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:34.133
Then invoices. The invoices sent in the date range, ready for QuickBooks' invoice import.

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:43.100
Payments. Payments received in the range, as a deposit list the bookkeeper matches to the bank. Click it when that's the file you need.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:50.633
From and To. The date range. It starts on the 1st of this month and runs to today; change either date.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:59.500
Only what wasn't exported yet. Leave it ticked so nothing goes into QuickBooks twice. Untick it to export the whole range again.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.733
Mark these as exported. Remembers what went into this file, so 'Only what wasn't exported yet' skips it next time.

00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:19.700
Make the file. Builds the file and shows its name and row count, with Download (a .csv file) and Copy. Then import it in QuickBooks. The tour doesn't make one.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.967
Close. The X closes the panel.

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:29.067
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
